.TH QUANUX-SPREADER 1 "FEBRUARY 2026" "QuanuX Biological Sovereignty" "QuanuX System Manual"
.SH NAME
quanux-spreader \- The Metabolic Enzyme (Execution Engine)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quanux-spreader
[\fB--config\fR \fIPATH\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBquanux-spreader\fR is the active catalyst of the QuanuX cell. It functions as the metabolic enzyme, processing raw sensory data ingested from the external synapses (NATS/Adapters) and converting it into "Trade-ATP" (Execution Packets).
.SH METABOLIC FUNCTIONS
The enzyme operates exclusively within tight execution loops (59ns). It does not hold state or possess an immune response; it strictly calculates and attempts to dispatch limit orders. 

Before execution reaches external markets, it must pass through the \fBSovereign Sentinel\fR (\fBritchie-interlock(2)\fR) for risk binding. This prevents rogue enzymatic activity from damaging the cellular organism.
.SH ENVIRONMENT AND CATALYSTS
The enzyme requires specific environmental scalars to function:
.IP \[ci] 3
.B QUANUX_MARKET_NATS
The address of the external sensory fluid (Market Data input stream).
.IP \[ci] 3
.B QUANUX_ORDER_ROUTING
The address of the execution synapse for order dispatch.
